                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_434">Oxford, Oxfordshire. St Mary
                        Magdalen College</orgName><p>‘Memorandum quod 29. die mensis Marcij Anno
                        domini 1469. Magister Willielmus Wagge quondam Rector ecclesie sancte marie
                        Wynton’ legauit hunc librum Magistro Willelmo Ive doctori in theologia ad
                        terminum vite sue sub hac condicione quod in recepcione eiusdem dicat
                        exequias et missam de Requie pro anima predicti Willielmum et animabus
                        omnium fidelium defunctorum Ita quod post ipsius Magistri Willielmi Ive
                        decessum dictus liber tradatur assignetur et committatur Cuidam honesto viro
                        et discreto Capellano sub prefata condicione et sic deinceps de viro in
                        virum quamdiu liber durauerit’(fol. 2r)William Ive was headmaster of
                        Winchester and an associate of William Waynflete’s. He donated at least two
                        other MSS to Magdalen and likely gave this as well, though there is no
                        evidence for its presence in the College before 1600.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Perhaps William Ive (d. 1486), headmaster of
                     Winchester College, master of Whittington College, London, and chancellor of
                     Salisbury</provenance>
